# Expense Tracker with Live Currency Conversion

People who travel, freelance internationally, or shop from foreign stores lose track of spending because every purchase is in a different currency. This single-page app lets you log each expense in the currency you actually paid in and instantly see everything, plus a running total, converted into one home currency using live exchange rates.

https://trevorayunga.github.io/Expense-Tracker/
## Features
- Add expenses (description, amount, currency, category)
- Each expense shows its original amount and its converted home-currency value
- Running total that updates on add, delete, filter, or home-currency change
- Delete expenses; filter by category; change home currency
- Loading and error states with a Retry button (the UI never silently breaks)
- Expenses without an available rate are flagged, not silently dropped

## Tech used
- REST API: [open.er-api.com](https://www.exchangerate-api.com/docs/free) (free, no key) via `fetch()` + `async/await`
- Vanilla JavaScript ES modules (`api`, `state`, `utils`, `ui`, `main`)
- Jest for unit tests
- ESLint (`eslint:recommended`)

## Run locally
npm install
npm start          # serves the site (ES modules need http://, not file://)
npm test           # run unit tests
npm run lint       # run ESLint
```

## Project structure
```
index.html, style.css
src/  api.js  state.js  utils.js  ui.js  main.js
tests/utils.test.js
```

- Component-level and end-to-end tests
